    parallel_grief_subtitle_refs: 'Iliad (Book XXIV) ↔ Epic of Gilgamesh (Tablet VIII)',
    parallel_grief_body: 'Both heroes lose their closest companion — Patroclus for Achilles, Enkidu for Gilgamesh. Both are left to confront mortality through the loss. The companion functions as the hero\'s alter-ego; the companion\'s death is the hinge on which heroic identity turns. The traditions diverge in what the hero does with that grief: Achilles accepts and restores relation; Gilgamesh refuses and seeks escape.',
