    tablet_hub_subtitle: 'The Flood Tablet',
    tablet_hub_intro: 'The best-preserved tablet of the Standard Babylonian Version. Lines 1–196 contain the flood narrative; the rest records Utnapishtim\'s challenge and Gilgamesh\'s failure, followed by a coda added in the 12th century BCE by Sîn-lēqi-unninni. This is the tablet that first established the Gilgamesh epic\'s importance to modern scholarship when George Smith identified it in 1872.',
